Fix XHTTP compatibility with Xray and imported extra settings.
Path/query handling: https://github.com/MetaCubeX/mihomo/pull/3318
Source commit: db520c0a35e2426b3828c9bd5a402c1140ad3c2a
Padding, ranges and extra import: https://github.com/getmikan/Citrus/pull/9
Padding failure report: https://github.com/MetaCubeX/mihomo/issues/3068

Split configured paths from their raw query and preserve both for every upload
and download request, including separate download settings. Server path matching
uses only the path. Query-bearing mihomo peers need this behavior at both ends.

Treat zero-ended padding and selected sc-* ranges as unset, applying the Xray
fallbacks: padding 100-1000 bytes, stream-up server interval 20-80 seconds,
30 buffered posts, 1000000 bytes per post and a 30 ms post interval. Reject a
post-size range with a zero minimum. Retain zero semantics for reuse settings.

Import numeric or string XHTTP extra ranges consistently. Read download XMUX
from xhttpSettings.xmux, with xhttpSettings.extra.xmux taking precedence.
This patch covers configuration and wire-format compatibility, retaining the
existing packet-up sending implementation and explicit reuse configuration.

Tests cover all XHTTP modes, separate download queries, zero/default and invalid
ranges, actual server acceptance of zero-configured padding, reuse zero values,
and the complete extra-link conversion through proxy construction.

